;The Empire Strikes Back (Atari, 1985) - hardware map, RAM variables and equates
;of the main 6809, for esb_bank0_rom.asm, esb_bank1_rom.asm, the four
;esb_slapstic*_rom.asm and esb_vector_rom.asm.
;Names carried over from the Star Wars source are Atari's identifiers ('.' -> '_'
;and '$' -> 'S_'), given to the address or value the same code uses here.
;Descriptions in upper case are Atari's comments on the Star Wars definitions;
;those in lower case were written for the Star Wars or for this disassembly.
;Generated by disasm/emit_defines.py; every symbol the listings use is here.

;----------------------------------[ Memory map ]----------------------------------
.alias VectorRam         $00      ;Through $2FFF. AVG display lists.
.alias VectorRom         $3000    ;Through $3FFF (esb_vector_rom.asm).
.alias InputPorts        $4300    ;Through $439F. Switch inputs $4300 and $4320, option switches $4340 and $4360, ADC $4380.
.alias SoundLatch        $4400    ;$4400 data to and from the sound CPU, $4401 the two ready flags.
.alias NvRam             $4500    ;Through $45FF. Non-volatile RAM: high scores and bookkeeping.
.alias OutputLatches     $4600    ;Through $46FF. VG go $4600, VG reset $4620, watchdog $4640, IRQ clear $4660, output bits $4680, NVRAM store $46A0, ADC channel $46C0, sound reset $46E0.
.alias MathBox           $4700    ;Through $4707. Matrix processor start and block index, divider; reads give the quotient and the random number.
.alias CpuRam            $4800    ;Through $4FFF. Program RAM; the direct page is here and the stack grows down from the top.
.alias MathRam           $5000    ;Through $5FFF. Matrix processor RAM, shared with the CPU.
.alias BankedRomLow      $6000    ;Through $7FFF. Bank 0 (esb_bank0_rom.asm) or bank 1 (esb_bank1_rom.asm), by W_BANK D7.
.alias SlapsticWindow    $8000    ;Through $9FFF. One of four pages, selected by the slapstic (esb_slapstic0_rom.asm .. 3).
.alias BankedRomHigh     $A000    ;Through $FFFF. Switched with $6000-$7FFF by W_BANK D7; each bank has its own 6809 vectors at $FFF2.

;----------------------------------[ Hardware registers ]----------------------------------
