.alias xmit_atst         $4A54    ;enemy record area with a different use in each part: the three $28-byte probot transmission records ($4A54-$4ACB, page 3 xmit_init on) in the probot part, the three AT-ST records of $11 bytes ($4A54-$4A86, page 1 atst_init on) in the walker part. byte 0 of a record is zero when it is free. the address is also the end of the five probot records at ALIEN
.alias atat_rec          $4A87    ;the three AT-AT records of the walker part, $19 bytes each up to cable_rec ($4AD2), kept by page 0 (atat_init on). byte 0 is the type, zero when the record is free, byte 1 the flags of the frame, 3 the shot delay, 4 the movement mode, 5-10 x, y and height, 11-16 where the head is from the centre, $11 and $13 the head's yaw and pitch angles, $15 the walk cycle counter, $16 the leg set. the address is also the end of the AT-ST records
.alias cable_rec         $4AD2    ;first byte of the tow cable's record, which follows the three AT-AT records (page 0, P0_9561 on): 0 while no cable is out, bit 3 set by P0_9915 once it has caught a walker's legs. byte 2 is its mode and byte 3 a timer. the AT-AT code tests it before letting the walkers go at the end of the part and before the leg catch test, and clears it when a caught walker blows up
.alias cable_mode        $4AD4    ;byte 2 of the tow cable's record cable_rec, its mode: 1 in flight (cable_fire), 2 once it has caught a walker (cable_attach). cable_move calls the mode's routine through cable_mode_tab
