.alias prob_hit_rec      $4C0F    ;word, goes with prob_hit_d: address of that probot's record, which probot_shot_down on page 2 then destroys. lz_hit_probot only splashes the lazar when it is 0
.alias atst_hit_d        $4C11    ;word: view distance of the nearest AT-ST the laser cursor is on in this frame, written by atst_body_hit and atst_window_hit while the AT-STs are drawn. the laser start on page 3 (P3_95CC) sets the high byte to $FF for none, and page 3 P3_97CB compares it with the distances of the other things under the cursor and takes the nearest
.alias atst_hit_rec      $4C13    ;word, goes with atst_hit_d: the record of the AT-ST whose front window the cursor is on, which atst_killed then destroys, or 0 when the nearest hit was on the body and the shot only stops there
.alias astr_hit_d        $4C15    ;word: view distance of the nearest asteroid the lazar cursor is on in this frame, written by page 2 P2_9BC3 while the asteroids are drawn. the lazar start (P3_95CF) sets the high byte to $FF for none, lz_hit_space compares it with the distances of the shots and the alien ships
.alias astr_hit_rec      $4C17    ;word, goes with astr_hit_d: page 2 P2_9BC3 only ever writes 0 here, so lz_hit_space always splashes the lazar against the asteroid
