.alias ind_flash         $4CA7    ;nonzero while a mark of the top indicator is changing: set to $7F with flash_fade by ind_flash_start, cleared when flash_fade has run out. in the probot part the new mark flashes in and is counted in prog_count at the end, and a transmission that gets through meanwhile is not counted. in the walker part the burst of the lost mark is drawn
.alias status_msg        $4CA8    ;number of the status message on the top line in the probot and walker parts: $34 or $3A at the start of the part, then chosen again every 32 frames from probot_msg_tab or walker_msg_tab by prog_count and the frame counter
.alias PH_YOF            $4CA9    ;Message Y offset of the current phase (scroll); copied to MSYOFF.
.alias PH_TIM            $4CAB    ;Phase timer: set by a phase's init entry and counted by its execute entry, which moves on when it runs out.
.alias ph_tim_lo         $4CAC    ;low byte of PH_TIM, the phase timer.
.alias PH_COL            $4CAD    ;Colour instruction for the current phase's messages; its brightness byte is stepped down to fade a page out.
.alias ph_col_brt        $4CAE    ;PH_COL+1, the brightness byte of the phase colour, where the listing shows it as a bare address: the attract pages step it down to fade their messages and the message drawing (mes_lines_fade) takes the brightness of every line from it
.alias w1_anim_pts       $4CAF    ;word: math RAM address (BJ_RAM) taken by the probot set-up after objects 4-7 are loaded, so the first of the 8-byte point records of objects 9-$10. P2_8E86 starts its per-frame point animation here
.alias w1_anim_end       $4CB1    ;word: math RAM address (BJ_RAM) taken by the probot set-up after object $10 is loaded, the end of the point records that P2_8E86 animates
.alias leg_obj           $4CB3    ;temp of P2_91CC: the object number, 9-$10, of the probot leg that goes with the mask bit being looked at
.alias leg_mask          $4CB4    ;temp of P2_91CC: the probot's part mask (byte $13 of its record), shifted right one bit for each leg until it is 0
.alias man_page          $4CB5    ;rebel training manual: page within the section, 0-2, shown as 1-3. stepped on by man_init_probot, so it changes once in every pass through the four sections
.alias man_script        $4CB6    ;rebel training manual: word, pointer to the next 8-byte record of the page's script (time word, command byte, operands). set by manual_page_init, stepped by manual_run
