.alias sc_add_top        $4CBA    ;SC_ADD-1: the top two BCD digits of the amount last added to the score, which is shown as 8 digits from here. zero except for the continued play bonus
.alias SC_ADD            $4CBB    ;AMOUNT BEING ADDED TO SCORE, BCD
.alias SC_ADT            $4CBE    ;TIMER FOR DISPLAYING ADDED AMOUNT
.alias legs_bonus        $4CBF    ;3 BCD bytes ($4CBF-$4CC1): the progressive bonus for flying through an AT-AT's legs. cleared by the walker part's setup, raised by 5,000 up to 900,000 and added to the score by scr_legs_bonus each time page 0 (P0_87DD) sees the player pass under a walker, shown while legs_bon_tmr runs
.alias legs_bonus_2      $4CC1    ;third byte of legs_bonus
.alias SP_COL            $4CC2    ;SPLASH COLOR
.alias SP_LOC            $4CC4    ;HI BYTE OF X DISTANCE AWAY
.alias SP_TYP            $4CC5    ;TYPE OF SPLASH, QUADS
.alias ST_UY             $4CC6    ;PLAYERS UNIVERSE Y FOR STARS
.alias ST_UZ             $4CC8    ;PLAYERS UNIVERSE Z FOR STARS
.alias snd_mute          $4CCA    ;nonzero mutes the sound effects: doxmt_gated, and bank 1's copy of it at K6530, send their command only while it is 0. the five dying phases set it to 1, the starting wave select, the continue offer, begin_act_init and PHEEGM clear it
.alias kill_count        $4CCB    ;AT-STs shot in a walker part, counted to 50 at most by atst_killed on page 1 (AT-ATs are not counted). cable_init on page 0 gives the next walker part 4 + count/5 tow cables, 9 at most, and clears it. cleared at game start
.alias exec_x            $4CCC    ;word: screen x of the Executor in the TIE fighter part, saved sign extended by VWDTHB from its projected centre. exec_drift_left moves it 16 to the left every frame in phase $2A, which ends when it is -520 or less
.alias exec_y            $4CCE    ;word: screen y of the Executor, saved by VWDTHB for exec_drift_left
.alias coin_spoken       $4CD0    ;Star Wars's COINSP: the credit count for which the coin sound was made. 0 with no credits, so the first credit sounds, then $FF once more credits have come in
.alias AM_PTR            $4CD1    ;AIM POINTER TO ALIEN BEING CHASED
.alias MUSTIM            $4CD3    ;FLAG FOR HEARING MUSIC DURING ATTRACT
.alias cont_nocrd        $4CD4    ;continue screen: set the first time the planet is fired on with no credit, when 256 frames are put back on the countdown, so that it happens once.
.alias w2_spk_cnt        $4CD5    ;wave 2: counts the frames a page 0 test (P0_8F45) holds running. At 20 the speech spk_cmd_03 is started and the count parks at $80. Cleared by the wave 2 setup.
.alias cables_used       $4CD6    ;tow cables fired in this walker part: cleared by the part's setup (page 0 P0_9561), counted up by page 0 P0_9596 for each cable fired. while it is 0 the loss of the first mark of the advance indicator sends speech $17
.alias hit_spk_done      $4CD7    ;wave 2: nonzero once the speech spk_cmd_09 has been started by page 0 (P0_9641), or is no longer wanted - the end of wave init bumps it.
.alias glow_said         $4CD8    ;set once the speech for a shot that hits the ship while its shield is already glowing has been sent (GNAHIT on page 1, P1_94D2: spk_cmd_19 in the probot and walker parts, spk_cmd_27 in the other two). cleared by the setups of the probot part and of the TIE fighter part only, so it is said once for each pair of parts
.alias hit_said          $4CD9    ;set at the first enemy shot that hits the ship in a part while the shield is not glowing and shields are left (GNAHIT on page 1, P1_94AB). in the TIE fighter and asteroid parts that hit sends a speech (spk_cmd_1d, spk_cmd_25), in the other two nothing. cleared by the setup of every part
